WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.013
[♪ opening theme music playing]

2
00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:14.556
[bird screeching]

3
00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.666
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

4
00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:44.920
[♪ gentle music playing]

5
00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:48.048
[soft footsteps echoing]

6
00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.869
Are you a good dancer, Your Majesty?

7
00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:29.464
I'd say so.

8
00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:40.434
Can you hold your own?

9
00:01:44.896 --> 00:01:46.690
I will glide along with you.

10
00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:12.507
[♪ music continues]

11
00:02:25.729 --> 00:02:27.105
[stammers] Wait…

12
00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:35.530
[stammers]

13
00:02:36.406 --> 00:02:37.908
-[Albani scoffs]
-If you step on my foot,

14
00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.451
I'll pretend not to notice.

15
00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:42.621
That won't happen, Your Highness.

16
00:02:42.704 --> 00:02:44.331
[chuckles] Do not worry.

17
00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:46.833
I'm very tight-lipped, Your Majesty.

18
00:02:55.258 --> 00:02:56.551
Dancing with you

19
00:02:57.469 --> 00:02:58.720
is truly my honor.

20
00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.021
[♪ slow waltz music playing]

21
00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:40.971
The honor is mine.

22
00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:44.182
Ladies have lost sleep, I'm certain…

23
00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:47.602
wondering with whom
you would share your first dance.

24
00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:52.816
Are you saying Your Majesty was not
looking forward to dancing with me?

25
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.777
Ah! Are you married by chance?

26
00:03:55.861 --> 00:03:57.946
[Navier chuckles]

27
00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.656
What a shame.

28
00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:26.016
[♪ music continues]

29
00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:43.867
[♪ music fades]

30
00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.833
[♪ dramatic music playing]

31
00:05:02.886 --> 00:05:04.888
[guests gasping, exclaiming]

32
00:05:05.555 --> 00:05:06.890
[noblewoman] He's so dashing.
Just look at him!

33
00:05:08.058 --> 00:05:10.101
[♪ music continues]

34
00:05:26.368 --> 00:05:27.869
Well done.

35
00:05:31.414 --> 00:05:32.415
Why?

36
00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:35.377
Just keep on looking at me like that.

37
00:05:46.972 --> 00:05:48.807
[♪ waltz music playing]

38
00:06:37.355 --> 00:06:39.107
[♪ music continues]

39
00:07:05.383 --> 00:07:06.593
[laughing]

40
00:07:39.584 --> 00:07:40.877
[♪ music swells]

41
00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:56.810
[♪ music fades]

42
00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:22.335
[guests cheering and clapping]

43
00:08:34.723 --> 00:08:35.890
[Laura giggling]

44
00:09:06.046 --> 00:09:08.506
[♪ gentle waltz music playing]

45
00:09:17.432 --> 00:09:18.767
May I have the next dance?

46
00:09:33.782 --> 00:09:34.783
What is she doing?

47
00:09:35.366 --> 00:09:36.785
Why is Ms. Rashta going over there?

48
00:09:37.202 --> 00:09:38.203
Don't do it.

49
00:09:41.748 --> 00:09:43.958
[Rashta] So, I was thinking…

50
00:09:44.042 --> 00:09:47.378
Rashta and Prince Heinrey can share
the next dance together.

51
00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:54.511
[chuckles awkwardly]

52
00:09:58.431 --> 00:09:59.682
Forgive me.

53
00:09:59.766 --> 00:10:03.311
I want to cherish the dance I shared
with Her Majesty as my last for today.

54
00:10:07.482 --> 00:10:10.193
[nobles snickering]

55
00:10:15.156 --> 00:10:16.741
What does she think she's doing?

56
00:10:16.825 --> 00:10:18.993
[gasps] Goodness! Ugh!

57
00:10:19.077 --> 00:10:20.453
Earlier…

58
00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:24.833
what were you discussing
with the Prince of the Western Kingdom?

59
00:10:24.916 --> 00:10:26.417
A few pleasantries, nothing more.

60
00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:27.961
[scoffs]

61
00:10:29.838 --> 00:10:33.216
Have you never heard the rumors
that circulate about him?

62
00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:35.927
How could you have an ordinary
conversation with a man like that?

63
00:10:36.511 --> 00:10:38.054
He is an amusing character.

64
00:10:38.138 --> 00:10:40.181
[scoffs] Being a notorious womanizer,

65
00:10:40.849 --> 00:10:41.975
I would imagine he is.

66
00:10:44.769 --> 00:10:46.938
I know some womanizers who are not.

67
00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:56.531
[clicks tongue, inhales]
Well, I suppose I cannot forbid you

68
00:10:56.614 --> 00:11:00.034
to take a lover of your own
since I have taken a mistress myself.

69
00:11:00.118 --> 00:11:01.161
Still…

70
00:11:02.203 --> 00:11:04.164
I wouldn't recommend Heinrey
as your choice.

71
00:11:04.873 --> 00:11:06.416
Would you please speak more plainly?

72
00:11:06.499 --> 00:11:08.459
If you carry on like this,

73
00:11:08.543 --> 00:11:10.670
I dare say you would not be
calling him your lover,

74
00:11:11.212 --> 00:11:15.258
but rather, it is yourself
who will be a mistress to this man.

75
00:11:17.927 --> 00:11:20.221
You know, you are the Empress of--

76
00:11:20.305 --> 00:11:22.473
I'm not certain I understand your meaning.

77
00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:25.977
However, nothing of that sort will happen.

78
00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:30.315
How wise of you.

79
00:11:30.398 --> 00:11:34.068
For the Empress to become
the object of reckless flirtation

80
00:11:34.152 --> 00:11:35.695
with a man who toys
with every woman he sees

81
00:11:35.778 --> 00:11:36.821
is not dignified.

82
00:11:39.199 --> 00:11:41.326
[♪ lively waltz music playing]

83
00:11:47.707 --> 00:11:49.000
[Rashta sobbing]

84
00:11:53.171 --> 00:11:54.631
[Rashta continues sobbing]

85
00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:55.798
Rashta.

86
00:11:58.009 --> 00:11:59.594
[Rashta continues sobbing]

87
00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:08.436
Rashta.

88
00:12:08.937 --> 00:12:11.022
Your Majesty. [whimpers]

89
00:12:11.105 --> 00:12:12.649
What is it?

90
00:12:12.732 --> 00:12:15.735
Never leave Rashta behind again.

91
00:12:15.818 --> 00:12:17.070
Oh, it's all right.

92
00:12:19.447 --> 00:12:21.074
Look at this.
What do you think is going on?

93
00:12:21.157 --> 00:12:22.200
Yes, what is it?

94
00:12:22.283 --> 00:12:25.662
Someone said she had the nerve
to spread a rumor about poor Rashta.

95
00:12:25.745 --> 00:12:28.373
-[gasps]
-Saying she was a runaway slave.

96
00:12:28.456 --> 00:12:29.874
Ah, well, even so!

97
00:12:29.958 --> 00:12:32.710
Who would have thought
the dignified Empress would do that?

98
00:12:32.794 --> 00:12:34.921
-[noblewoman 1] What did I tell you?
-[noblewoman 2] That is so scary.

99
00:12:35.004 --> 00:12:37.090
-[noblewoman 3] Her Majesty is jealous!
-[noblewoman 2] That's so scary.

100
00:12:37.173 --> 00:12:39.050
[noblewoman 3]
They say Her Majesty has actually been

101
00:12:39.133 --> 00:12:41.219
showering that woman
with all kinds of gifts.

102
00:12:41.302 --> 00:12:43.554
You're saying behind the scenes,
she's scheming?

103
00:12:43.638 --> 00:12:45.556
-Oh! How embarrassing.
-[all laughing]

104
00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:47.767
-I guess it shows what she's really like.
-Oh!

105
00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:48.851
[exclaims]

106
00:12:48.935 --> 00:12:50.478
-Oh! Oh, oh.
-What is this?

107
00:12:50.561 --> 00:12:51.604
Are you all right?

108
00:12:51.688 --> 00:12:53.356
[stammering]

109
00:12:53.982 --> 00:12:56.150
Oh, Your… Your Highness.

110
00:12:56.234 --> 00:12:57.694
[giggles nervously] I'm fine.

111
00:12:57.777 --> 00:12:59.195
Yeah.

112
00:12:59.279 --> 00:13:00.446
Why'd you push?

113
00:13:02.824 --> 00:13:03.950
It was a mistake.

114
00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:05.785
Sorry, Your Majesty.

115
00:13:05.868 --> 00:13:07.996
Oh, honestly, that made me startled.

116
00:13:08.079 --> 00:13:10.039
[sighs] So sorry.

117
00:13:10.123 --> 00:13:11.165
[giggles]

118
00:13:11.249 --> 00:13:12.875
[indistinct conversation]

119
00:13:12.959 --> 00:13:14.544
[Rashta laughing]

120
00:13:15.586 --> 00:13:17.380
Just look at those two over there.

121
00:13:18.089 --> 00:13:20.758
Why is she walking around
as though she's the host?

122
00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:23.553
This New Year's Ceremony
is something Her Majesty prepared

123
00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:25.096
with everything she had.

124
00:13:29.934 --> 00:13:32.186
[♪ moody music playing]

125
00:13:46.784 --> 00:13:47.869
[birds chirping]

126
00:14:10.016 --> 00:14:11.100
[wings flapping]

127
00:14:13.561 --> 00:14:14.854
[♪ bright, playful music playing]

128
00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:18.066
[chuckles] Queen!

129
00:14:18.149 --> 00:14:19.692
[chirping]

130
00:14:19.776 --> 00:14:21.194
[chuckles softly] Will you join?

131
00:14:23.071 --> 00:14:24.238
[laughing]

132
00:14:26.157 --> 00:14:27.575
[bird chirping]

133
00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:30.912
Your Highness.

134
00:14:34.248 --> 00:14:35.333
[chirps]

135
00:14:35.416 --> 00:14:37.335
What are you doing here?

136
00:14:38.169 --> 00:14:39.837
-Go away!
-[bird chirps in surprise]

137
00:14:41.089 --> 00:14:42.548
[bird screeches]

138
00:14:42.632 --> 00:14:44.675
[Queen chirping]

139
00:14:46.177 --> 00:14:47.261
[chuckles] What's wrong?

140
00:14:55.478 --> 00:14:56.604
[sighs]

141
00:14:56.687 --> 00:14:58.272
Let me hold you, Queen.

142
00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:01.859
[♪ gentle music playing]

143
00:15:03.778 --> 00:15:04.779
Mmm.

144
00:15:05.613 --> 00:15:07.240
-You're warm, Queen.
-[chirps]

145
00:15:07.323 --> 00:15:08.324
Thank you…

146
00:15:09.992 --> 00:15:11.119
for being here.

147
00:15:14.038 --> 00:15:15.790
I have strength because of you.

148
00:15:17.083 --> 00:15:19.043
[♪ happy music playing]

149
00:15:19.127 --> 00:15:20.545
[chirping]

150
00:15:20.628 --> 00:15:22.463
[chuckles softly]

151
00:15:27.135 --> 00:15:28.845
You're very human-like.

152
00:15:30.221 --> 00:15:31.472
[chirps]

153
00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.102
You'll return home soon.

154
00:15:36.185 --> 00:15:38.646
Once the Ceremony ends,
you'll go back with your master.

155
00:15:40.648 --> 00:15:42.233
What will I do without you?

156
00:15:43.734 --> 00:15:44.735
[chirps]

157
00:15:45.444 --> 00:15:46.445
Hmm?

158
00:15:50.908 --> 00:15:52.160
[Heinrey] "Let's wager Queen."

159
00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:54.036
[gasps]

160
00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:55.621
Queen…

161
00:15:56.247 --> 00:15:57.373
the note says to wager you.

162
00:16:00.042 --> 00:16:03.296
"P.S. You did attend the Ceremony,
did you not?

163
00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.799
Perhaps you were among the…

164
00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:09.343
ladies that I danced with."

165
00:16:23.649 --> 00:16:25.985
Are you a good dancer, Your Majesty?

166
00:16:36.579 --> 00:16:38.206
[♪ captivating music playing]

167
00:16:46.088 --> 00:16:47.340
It couldn't be…

168
00:16:48.758 --> 00:16:49.967
Prince Heinrey?

169
00:16:52.303 --> 00:16:53.638
I don't believe it.

170
00:16:57.433 --> 00:16:58.768
No, surely not.

171
00:16:58.851 --> 00:17:00.811
[chirping]

172
00:17:03.064 --> 00:17:05.066
[Navier] "I did attend
the New Year's Ceremony,

173
00:17:05.149 --> 00:17:07.276
"but regrettably, I am a man."

174
00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:08.361
[chirps]

175
00:17:09.737 --> 00:17:10.738
[chuckles softly]

176
00:17:12.073 --> 00:17:13.282
This way, I'm hidden.

177
00:17:13.866 --> 00:17:15.243
What do you think?

178
00:17:15.326 --> 00:17:17.578
Now he won't discover my identity.

179
00:17:17.662 --> 00:17:18.829
-[chirps]
-[chuckles softly]

180
00:17:18.913 --> 00:17:20.748
[♪ calming music playing]

181
00:17:20.831 --> 00:17:22.250
Your master's intriguing.

182
00:17:22.959 --> 00:17:24.293
I'd like to know him more.

183
00:17:25.544 --> 00:17:26.879
And I wish dearly

184
00:17:27.463 --> 00:17:29.882
that I could win this bet
so you were mine.

185
00:17:30.925 --> 00:17:31.926
[chirps]

186
00:17:39.141 --> 00:17:42.311
However, my position will not allow
such freedom.

187
00:17:51.153 --> 00:17:52.905
-[Queen screeches]
-[♪ music continues]

188
00:17:57.159 --> 00:17:58.452
[whooshing]

189
00:18:14.093 --> 00:18:15.219
[Heinrey sighs]

190
00:18:17.096 --> 00:18:19.098
[♪ soft music playing]

191
00:18:19.765 --> 00:18:23.644
"A fate that had lost its way found me,
and now I send it back."

192
00:18:23.728 --> 00:18:24.770
[huffs]

193
00:18:24.854 --> 00:18:27.940
"Come to think of it, the bird's eyes
are the same purple as the…

194
00:18:29.859 --> 00:18:31.736
"flower petals."

195
00:18:33.029 --> 00:18:34.488
No wonder…

196
00:18:36.365 --> 00:18:39.410
The look in your eyes while
you were dancing was rather intense.

197
00:18:39.994 --> 00:18:42.538
It turns out you were out
searching for your "fate,"

198
00:18:42.622 --> 00:18:45.333
when I thought you were just out scouting.

199
00:18:48.044 --> 00:18:49.712
Sort your clothes out, will you?

200
00:18:49.795 --> 00:18:51.547
Don't speak of my "fate"
looking like that.

201
00:18:51.631 --> 00:18:53.507
-[zipper zips loudly]
-[chuckles]

202
00:18:54.133 --> 00:18:55.176
Is it true?

203
00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:56.927
Don't tell me that you…

204
00:18:57.678 --> 00:18:58.679
You…

205
00:18:58.763 --> 00:19:00.014
have feelings for her?

206
00:19:00.097 --> 00:19:01.265
Empress Navier?

207
00:19:01.349 --> 00:19:03.643
You honestly have to tell me
the truth immediately.

208
00:19:05.645 --> 00:19:08.939
Now, if I'm honest about how I feel,

209
00:19:09.023 --> 00:19:11.233
I worry that you would cry.

210
00:19:11.317 --> 00:19:12.693
Uh, cry?

211
00:19:12.777 --> 00:19:14.654
What exactly are you
saying to me right now?

212
00:19:15.237 --> 00:19:16.405
What?

213
00:19:16.489 --> 00:19:17.782
Your Highness,

214
00:19:17.865 --> 00:19:20.868
if you want a romance which is serious,
I am all for it.

215
00:19:20.951 --> 00:19:23.120
However, if that woman is her…

216
00:19:23.204 --> 00:19:26.999
If you've fallen in love with the Empress,
then that is another problem altogether.

217
00:19:27.083 --> 00:19:29.960
She's the empress of a powerful empire!

218
00:19:30.044 --> 00:19:32.505
Even if it was a tiny little empire,
it's still an issue.

219
00:19:32.588 --> 00:19:34.715
How could you do this to me?
I am mortified!

220
00:19:34.799 --> 00:19:36.801
Surely you wouldn't want
to become entangled

221
00:19:36.884 --> 00:19:39.261
in a scandal of passion
with the Eastern Empire?

222
00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:42.640
Oh, wouldn't I?

223
00:19:45.601 --> 00:19:48.771
It looks as though
the Emperor has fallen for another.

224
00:19:48.854 --> 00:19:49.939
Now then…

225
00:19:50.022 --> 00:19:52.483
the Empress surely wouldn't embrace
and forgive this.

226
00:19:53.734 --> 00:19:56.153
And that is because she could leave him
for me instead…

227
00:19:56.237 --> 00:19:58.155
Even if the Emperor
has fallen for another,

228
00:19:58.239 --> 00:20:00.032
she is only the man's mistress.

229
00:20:00.116 --> 00:20:02.618
Do you think the Empress,
who possesses this great empire,

230
00:20:02.702 --> 00:20:04.787
would divorce her husband
over a single mistress?

231
00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.205
And the Emperor, too.

232
00:20:06.288 --> 00:20:08.457
Do you think
he would cast aside an Empress

233
00:20:08.541 --> 00:20:09.875
praised by all the other kingdoms?

234
00:20:09.959 --> 00:20:12.545
Will he raise a runaway slave
to the heights of Empress?

235
00:20:12.628 --> 00:20:17.174
Well, the fact that another woman
could catch his eye at all,

236
00:20:17.258 --> 00:20:19.969
even though Navier is amazing,
it proves he's insane.

237
00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:21.679
Uh, no. Out of everyone…

238
00:20:21.762 --> 00:20:23.639
Out of all the great people of this Empire

239
00:20:23.723 --> 00:20:25.725
and all the guests who attended
the New Year's Ceremony,

240
00:20:25.808 --> 00:20:28.310
the craziest of all,
Prince Heinrey, it's you.

241
00:20:28.853 --> 00:20:31.981
[gasps and sighs melodramatically]

242
00:20:32.064 --> 00:20:33.399
Oh, what is this?

243
00:20:38.279 --> 00:20:39.280
It was a joke.

244
00:20:40.573 --> 00:20:42.491
I was just teasing, so you would cry.

245
00:20:43.075 --> 00:20:44.076
Ugh, you were?

246
00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:46.370
-Mmm-hmm.
-You were! [laughs]

247
00:20:46.912 --> 00:20:49.206
Ah, you, you scared me! [chuckles]

248
00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:51.375
-Let's prepare the talks.
-Yes, Your Highness.

249
00:20:57.882 --> 00:20:59.425
[people chattering]

250
00:21:02.511 --> 00:21:03.721
[indistinct shouting]

251
00:21:05.723 --> 00:21:08.934
EASTERN EMPIRE IMPERIAL GAZETTE
PRINCE HEINREY, NEW YEAR'S SENSATION

252
00:21:09.018 --> 00:21:11.103
TAKING HIGH SOCIETY BY STORM!
MISTRESS RASHTA BOTULIN

253
00:21:15.399 --> 00:21:18.819
[woman] To me, Her Majesty
the Empress is the most impressive.

254
00:21:18.903 --> 00:21:22.573
Someone described her as noble ice,
and that is exactly right!

255
00:21:22.656 --> 00:21:24.742
-[woman 1 laughs]
-[woman 2] Exactly!

256
00:21:24.825 --> 00:21:26.660
When I saw her, I froze like ice!

257
00:21:26.744 --> 00:21:28.662
Her aura was so overwhelming.

258
00:21:28.746 --> 00:21:29.997
-[woman 1] I know what you mean!
-[both laugh]

259
00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.123
MISS RASHTA'S STYLE

260
00:21:32.875 --> 00:21:34.585
-[door opens]
-[store owner] Okay.

261
00:21:34.668 --> 00:21:37.129
-Ah! Did you see it?
-Please don't touch that.

262
00:21:37.213 --> 00:21:38.798
-It's lovely.
-Look with your eyes only.

263
00:21:40.591 --> 00:21:42.426
Rashta… this girl…

264
00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:43.636
[chuckles]

265
00:21:45.054 --> 00:21:46.055
Who is she?

266
00:21:48.224 --> 00:21:49.558
What "girl"?

267
00:21:49.642 --> 00:21:50.726
She's the mistress.

268
00:21:51.435 --> 00:21:54.313
His Majesty the Emperor just acquired her.

269
00:21:54.396 --> 00:21:56.023
Rashta Ishka Botulin.

270
00:21:57.191 --> 00:21:58.234
A mistress?

271
00:21:58.901 --> 00:22:01.111
[laughs maliciously]

272
00:22:01.195 --> 00:22:02.196
Really?

273
00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:03.781
Ah!

274
00:22:03.864 --> 00:22:06.116
[store owner] Here's the item you ordered.

275
00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:07.660
[♪ ominous music playing]

276
00:22:22.424 --> 00:22:23.467
You've got this!

277
00:22:24.134 --> 00:22:26.136
[♪ bright music playing]

278
00:22:30.099 --> 00:22:32.768
[maid] The Grand Duchess Albani
has arrived.

279
00:22:35.437 --> 00:22:36.647
Look at you, child!

280
00:22:36.730 --> 00:22:38.399
You grow more radiant by the day.

281
00:22:38.983 --> 00:22:42.319
Fortunately, with all these events,
I can practice what I've learnt.

282
00:22:42.403 --> 00:22:43.863
[Albani] That is fortunate.

283
00:22:43.946 --> 00:22:45.865
So, keep enjoying yourself. Ha!

284
00:22:52.288 --> 00:22:55.332
Anyone would think
she belongs in high society.

285
00:22:56.125 --> 00:22:57.334
Keep quiet, girl.

286
00:22:57.418 --> 00:23:00.087
Goodness, all the grime washed right off.

287
00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:02.089
That expression…

288
00:23:02.172 --> 00:23:04.842
Isn't she imitating the Empress?

289
00:23:04.925 --> 00:23:07.678
Sometimes, Ms. Rashta
is rather disconcerting.

290
00:23:07.761 --> 00:23:11.473
It's almost as though her innocence
is all an act to bewitch people.

291
00:23:13.851 --> 00:23:15.019
What do you think?

292
00:23:17.271 --> 00:23:18.856
The Empress, do I look like her?

293
00:23:19.732 --> 00:23:23.027
-Oh, you are far more beautiful!
-[Kisia] Much more!

294
00:23:23.110 --> 00:23:25.446
[all giggling]

295
00:23:28.365 --> 00:23:30.784
Oh my! Oh, my goodness!

296
00:23:30.868 --> 00:23:33.537
It's so incredibly beautiful!

297
00:23:33.621 --> 00:23:36.290
Grand Duke Krom sent me a present.
How kind.

298
00:23:36.373 --> 00:23:37.374
Oh, did he?

299
00:23:37.458 --> 00:23:39.376
You really are building
close relationships

300
00:23:39.460 --> 00:23:40.502
with the foreign guests lately.

301
00:23:40.586 --> 00:23:41.962
You heard right.

302
00:23:42.046 --> 00:23:45.215
-Rashta is just adored by all foreigners.
-Mmm.

303
00:23:45.299 --> 00:23:48.928
A lady said to me that she heard
some of the guests say this.

304
00:23:49.511 --> 00:23:53.432
"He who moves the world
is the Emperor of the Eastern Empire,

305
00:23:53.515 --> 00:23:54.683
"and Rashta…

306
00:23:54.767 --> 00:23:57.478
"Rashta is the woman
who can move that Emperor."

307
00:23:57.561 --> 00:23:58.854
-[♪ music stops]
-[Rashta giggles]

308
00:23:59.605 --> 00:24:00.606
Shh!

309
00:24:00.689 --> 00:24:03.150
You mustn't say such things
out loud so carelessly.

310
00:24:03.859 --> 00:24:05.027
I only said it as a joke.

311
00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:07.363
[scoffs] It is not a joke
in the slightest.

312
00:24:07.446 --> 00:24:10.282
There would be serious trouble
if the court heard.

313
00:24:12.368 --> 00:24:14.578
Oh. I'll remember those words.

314
00:24:16.080 --> 00:24:17.081
Oh, well…

315
00:24:17.581 --> 00:24:20.751
I suppose as long as it has no direct
connection to the Emperor,

316
00:24:21.335 --> 00:24:23.045
then it is a very good thing.

317
00:24:23.128 --> 00:24:25.172
People should talk about you.

318
00:24:26.882 --> 00:24:28.425
Oh, I see now.

319
00:24:28.509 --> 00:24:29.551
[chuckles softly]

320
00:24:30.177 --> 00:24:31.720
Today, at last,

321
00:24:31.804 --> 00:24:34.682
the invitations to your banquet are ready!

322
00:24:34.765 --> 00:24:35.849
[♪ bright music playing]

323
00:24:35.933 --> 00:24:37.101
[squeals happily]

324
00:24:42.856 --> 00:24:43.857
[continues squealing]

325
00:24:43.941 --> 00:24:45.734
[both squealing, laughing]

326
00:24:47.987 --> 00:24:52.282
"We invite you to the banquet
of Rashta Ishka Botulin."

327
00:24:52.366 --> 00:24:54.159
[gasps] Oh!

328
00:24:54.243 --> 00:24:55.494
Do you think people will go?

329
00:24:56.078 --> 00:24:57.871
Oh, my goodness! I'm so nervous!

330
00:24:57.955 --> 00:25:00.541
-[laughing]
-[Albani chuckles awkwardly]

331
00:25:00.624 --> 00:25:02.835
[Philomena] The noble ladies
are gasping for attention

332
00:25:02.918 --> 00:25:04.878
from the guests at the West Palace.

333
00:25:04.962 --> 00:25:06.797
[Albani] Poor little Rashta,
she's so excited,

334
00:25:06.880 --> 00:25:09.216
but this banquet won't amount to much.

335
00:25:09.842 --> 00:25:11.343
The noble ladies…

336
00:25:11.427 --> 00:25:13.470
-they won't dare attend.
-[♪ ominous music playing]

337
00:25:13.554 --> 00:25:15.389
It would be the ultimate betrayal.

338
00:25:16.140 --> 00:25:17.975
And the Empress still has their loyalty.

339
00:25:18.684 --> 00:25:21.520
Abandoning her because
they were swayed by some fleeting rumor?

340
00:25:21.603 --> 00:25:23.480
Honestly… They won't do that.

341
00:25:24.064 --> 00:25:26.942
Then why did you say
you would hold a banquet for Ms. Rashta?

342
00:25:27.651 --> 00:25:28.944
If the company is lacking,

343
00:25:29.028 --> 00:25:31.780
the Botulin House
will suffer a blow as well.

344
00:25:31.864 --> 00:25:34.199
We are finally regaining entry
into high society

345
00:25:34.283 --> 00:25:36.410
after being barred for 15 years.

346
00:25:36.493 --> 00:25:38.287
The pieces are all set for us.

347
00:25:38.370 --> 00:25:39.538
Finally, we can join the game.

348
00:25:42.916 --> 00:25:44.752
You know what our goal is.

349
00:25:44.835 --> 00:25:46.920
It is not to elevate Rashta.

350
00:25:48.422 --> 00:25:50.549
It is Navier's complete torment.

351
00:25:50.632 --> 00:25:53.802
To destroy that woman's soul
and her glowing reputation with it.

352
00:25:54.803 --> 00:25:56.680
We will isolate her entirely.

353
00:25:56.764 --> 00:25:58.140
[♪ soft music playing]

354
00:26:09.777 --> 00:26:11.153
[rattling]

355
00:26:13.072 --> 00:26:14.740
[screeches]

356
00:26:16.408 --> 00:26:18.077
Oh! [laughs]

357
00:26:20.329 --> 00:26:21.330
[chirps]

358
00:26:21.914 --> 00:26:23.457
[chuckles] Queen!

359
00:26:23.540 --> 00:26:25.084
He's so funny.

360
00:26:25.167 --> 00:26:26.168
He flew over that way,

361
00:26:26.251 --> 00:26:27.836
and when he saw you were changing,
Your Majesty…

362
00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:31.256
he got so startled and scrambled
hurriedly to turn his back!

363
00:26:31.340 --> 00:26:32.341
[Eliza] I saw it, too.

364
00:26:32.424 --> 00:26:35.511
He looked ashamed, almost.
But that's silly, isn't it?

365
00:26:35.594 --> 00:26:37.096
[Laura] Yes, I know!

366
00:26:38.305 --> 00:26:39.389
[chuckles softly]

367
00:26:39.473 --> 00:26:41.183
You can look now, I'm decent.

368
00:26:46.647 --> 00:26:47.940
[Navier chuckles]

369
00:26:48.649 --> 00:26:50.234
Oh, did that make you shy?

370
00:26:50.317 --> 00:26:51.819
[chirping]

371
00:26:55.280 --> 00:26:56.990
[chirping]

372
00:27:02.204 --> 00:27:04.331
[Heinrey] "Are you even searching for me?"

373
00:27:17.928 --> 00:27:19.429
[Navier] "I'm searching hard.

374
00:27:19.513 --> 00:27:21.557
[♪ serene, enthralling music playing]

375
00:27:27.312 --> 00:27:28.397
"And you?

376
00:27:33.110 --> 00:27:34.111
"Are you looking for me?"

377
00:27:38.991 --> 00:27:43.120
I'M SEARCHING HARD.
AND YOU? ARE YOU LOOKING FOR ME?

378
00:28:04.182 --> 00:28:06.184
[♪ music continues]

379
00:28:33.420 --> 00:28:34.713
[McKenna] Wow!

380
00:28:35.297 --> 00:28:38.258
These Eastern Empire rascals
did a great job with the place.

381
00:28:38.342 --> 00:28:40.135
Have you visited the pond out there yet?

382
00:28:40.218 --> 00:28:42.804
The landscaping, ah, stunning!

383
00:28:42.888 --> 00:28:45.015
And my goodness, out front! Is it a lake?

384
00:28:45.098 --> 00:28:46.516
Is it the sea, perhaps?

385
00:28:46.600 --> 00:28:47.851
It's massive either way.

386
00:28:49.478 --> 00:28:51.229
-[♪ bright, playful music playing]
-McKenna!

387
00:28:51.313 --> 00:28:52.564
Yes?

388
00:28:52.648 --> 00:28:54.441
Who here cannot keep a secret?

389
00:28:55.025 --> 00:28:56.151
What was that?

390
00:28:57.277 --> 00:28:58.278
A secret?

391
00:28:58.362 --> 00:28:59.988
I need something circulating.

392
00:29:00.072 --> 00:29:02.366
It needs to be powerful and quick.

393
00:29:04.117 --> 00:29:05.994
The ministers of each nation
are moving forward

394
00:29:06.078 --> 00:29:07.412
with full-scale trade agreements.

395
00:29:07.496 --> 00:29:08.914
Our merchants are the most active,

396
00:29:08.997 --> 00:29:12.626
and the number of concluded agreements
is overwhelmingly high.

397
00:29:12.709 --> 00:29:14.461
Which nation has the second-highest trade?

398
00:29:14.544 --> 00:29:15.712
The Western Kingdom, Sire.

399
00:29:16.505 --> 00:29:18.006
Heinrey…

400
00:29:19.466 --> 00:29:21.885
Why did the king send the Prince
and not himself?

401
00:29:21.969 --> 00:29:23.470
It seems the rumors concerning

402
00:29:23.553 --> 00:29:26.682
King Walton III's grave illness are true.

403
00:29:26.765 --> 00:29:29.101
He swore he would punish us one day…

404
00:29:29.810 --> 00:29:32.980
because of all the humiliation
he suffered at our hand.

405
00:29:33.063 --> 00:29:35.273
Since he has no heirs with Queen Krista,

406
00:29:35.357 --> 00:29:38.986
it appears Prince Heinrey will succeed
to the throne as first in line.

407
00:29:39.069 --> 00:29:41.655
Huh. Wasn't there also
a matter of negotiation?

408
00:29:41.738 --> 00:29:45.075
Ah, there is a request for talks
on the port issue.

409
00:29:45.158 --> 00:29:48.203
We still have more of
the New Year's Ceremony to attend to.

410
00:29:49.663 --> 00:29:50.998
It would be burdensome

411
00:29:51.081 --> 00:29:53.250
to discuss with every nation watching.

412
00:29:53.333 --> 00:29:54.418
I concur.

413
00:29:56.753 --> 00:29:57.754
Let us conclude.

414
00:29:57.838 --> 00:30:00.549
I would like to have a discussion
with the empress alone.

415
00:30:00.632 --> 00:30:02.217
[chairs scraping]

416
00:30:09.141 --> 00:30:10.183
[door closes]

417
00:30:10.976 --> 00:30:12.269
[Sovieshu sighs]

418
00:30:14.021 --> 00:30:15.272
It's about Rashta.

419
00:30:15.981 --> 00:30:20.193
I hear the Botulin House
is holding a banquet in her honor.

420
00:30:20.736 --> 00:30:21.903
I heard, Your Majesty.

421
00:30:23.530 --> 00:30:25.282
What if you were able to attend it?

422
00:30:26.366 --> 00:30:27.701
Would you consider it?

423
00:30:30.454 --> 00:30:32.664
Even if the noble ladies wish
to accept Rashta,

424
00:30:32.748 --> 00:30:36.084
they are reluctant because
they are wary of your reaction.

425
00:30:40.047 --> 00:30:41.882
I have no plans to attend the banquet.

426
00:30:42.758 --> 00:30:44.718
If that is all you wish to say to me,

427
00:30:45.343 --> 00:30:46.344
I will take my leave.

428
00:30:53.393 --> 00:30:55.395
Were you always such a jealous person?

429
00:30:55.896 --> 00:30:57.564
If this is not jealousy,

430
00:30:59.232 --> 00:31:00.442
then what is it?

431
00:31:00.942 --> 00:31:03.361
You have strength and power as the Empress

432
00:31:03.445 --> 00:31:06.198
far beyond anything
Rashta could ever hope to match.

433
00:31:06.281 --> 00:31:09.326
And yet, you are treating
this powerless child

434
00:31:09.910 --> 00:31:12.079
as if she were your rival in love.

435
00:31:12.162 --> 00:31:13.830
Won't you open your heart to her?

436
00:31:16.166 --> 00:31:18.251
[♪ tense music playing]

437
00:31:20.003 --> 00:31:21.046
Oh, no.

438
00:31:22.756 --> 00:31:24.091
Your Majesty's mistress

439
00:31:24.841 --> 00:31:26.551
is no rival of mine.

440
00:31:27.761 --> 00:31:29.638
You may deem her precious.

441
00:31:30.430 --> 00:31:32.933
Do you expect me to share that sentiment?

442
00:31:34.309 --> 00:31:36.103
She is just a stranger to me, sire.

443
00:31:37.187 --> 00:31:38.730
And will remain as such.

444
00:31:39.481 --> 00:31:41.149
Do not involve me in this.

445
00:31:41.983 --> 00:31:43.944
These concerns will remain yours.

446
00:31:50.200 --> 00:31:52.160
My line is now drawn.

447
00:31:53.829 --> 00:31:55.038
I will hear no more.

448
00:31:57.707 --> 00:31:59.167
[scoffs softly]

449
00:32:00.293 --> 00:32:02.838
[♪ music intensifies]

450
00:32:05.549 --> 00:32:07.008
[clears throat]

451
00:32:11.555 --> 00:32:13.181
His Majesty is thirsty.

452
00:32:13.265 --> 00:32:14.432
[door closes]

453
00:32:16.476 --> 00:32:17.644
-Ah--
-[both sigh contentedly]

454
00:32:18.603 --> 00:32:19.771
[clears throat]

455
00:32:22.107 --> 00:32:23.191
[loud clattering]

456
00:32:24.025 --> 00:32:25.152
Lante!

457
00:32:25.735 --> 00:32:27.612
Yes! Yes, Your Majesty.

458
00:32:27.696 --> 00:32:30.574
Here, cold water! Cold water is here.

459
00:32:30.657 --> 00:32:31.741
[groans softly]

460
00:32:32.325 --> 00:32:34.202
[♪ gentle music playing]

461
00:32:34.286 --> 00:32:36.163
[woman] Your Majesty.

462
00:32:39.958 --> 00:32:42.210
Thank you for coming, Your Majesty.

463
00:32:42.294 --> 00:32:44.254
I've brought something for the bazaar.

464
00:32:44.337 --> 00:32:46.047
I hope this will suffice.

465
00:32:52.137 --> 00:32:53.680
How kind of you.

466
00:32:53.763 --> 00:32:55.640
I know the farmers are grateful.

467
00:32:56.892 --> 00:32:58.852
The support for the drought
is appreciated.

468
00:33:00.437 --> 00:33:03.982
As expected, Princess Circe,
your party is quite the popular one.

469
00:33:04.065 --> 00:33:05.483
Well, Your Majesty is here…

470
00:33:08.195 --> 00:33:10.530
and Prince Heinrey has graced us as well.

471
00:33:10.614 --> 00:33:12.282
That guarantees success.

472
00:33:14.075 --> 00:33:15.535
How fascinating!

473
00:33:15.619 --> 00:33:18.788
Wherever the prince goes,
a cloud of people always follow.

474
00:33:18.872 --> 00:33:20.498
He was already popular,

475
00:33:20.582 --> 00:33:23.376
but since the public notice
he released, well…

476
00:33:23.460 --> 00:33:25.212
now he's even more so.

477
00:33:25.295 --> 00:33:26.296
A public notice?

478
00:33:26.880 --> 00:33:28.089
Have you not heard?

479
00:33:29.841 --> 00:33:30.967
It's very exciting.

480
00:33:31.509 --> 00:33:33.345
There's someone in the Eastern Empire

481
00:33:33.428 --> 00:33:35.597
who's been exchanging
anonymous letters with Prince Heinrey.

482
00:33:36.181 --> 00:33:39.726
The South Palace has been ablaze
with talk of it since this morning.

483
00:33:39.809 --> 00:33:41.978
He's desperate to find that person
no matter what,

484
00:33:42.562 --> 00:33:43.605
even publicly if he must,

485
00:33:44.189 --> 00:33:46.358
and has asked people to spread the word.

486
00:33:46.441 --> 00:33:48.235
[♪ soft, heart-fluttering music playing]

487
00:34:00.121 --> 00:34:01.331
Are you quite well?

488
00:34:01.414 --> 00:34:02.791
[noblewoman] Princess Circe!

489
00:34:04.626 --> 00:34:05.627
One moment.

490
00:34:06.378 --> 00:34:08.421
[chuckles] You're here!

491
00:34:10.757 --> 00:34:14.135
[Laura] Your Majesty, don't you think
the master of that messenger bird

492
00:34:14.219 --> 00:34:15.637
might be Prince Heinrey?

493
00:34:15.720 --> 00:34:17.722
I had exactly the same idea.

494
00:34:17.806 --> 00:34:20.100
[Verdi] He's talking about you,
Your Majesty.

495
00:34:20.183 --> 00:34:22.018
You should speak to him right away.

496
00:34:22.102 --> 00:34:23.812
Prince Heinrey will be delighted

497
00:34:23.895 --> 00:34:26.940
to find out that you were
his correspondent, Your Majesty.

498
00:34:27.524 --> 00:34:29.818
And after all, he did ask you for a dance.

499
00:34:37.450 --> 00:34:40.745
It's prudent for me
to stay an anonymous friend.

500
00:34:41.705 --> 00:34:42.747
But then…

501
00:34:42.831 --> 00:34:45.917
He is surrounded
by many scandals involving women,

502
00:34:46.001 --> 00:34:47.752
so remaining cautious is wise.

503
00:34:47.836 --> 00:34:51.965
The people on the other side
are already inventing groundless rumors.

504
00:34:52.048 --> 00:34:55.385
If it comes to light that Her Majesty
has been privately exchanging letters

505
00:34:55.468 --> 00:34:56.511
with the prince…

506
00:34:56.594 --> 00:35:01.057
Ah. I suppose it would be like
a pack of wolves tearing into their prey.

507
00:35:01.141 --> 00:35:02.350
[Verdi] But it's just…

508
00:35:03.101 --> 00:35:04.811
it's just such a pity.

509
00:35:07.188 --> 00:35:08.815
Please do enjoy yourselves.

510
00:35:09.441 --> 00:35:12.402
I'll be searching for a present
for my mother.

511
00:35:12.485 --> 00:35:13.653
Yes.

512
00:35:15.488 --> 00:35:16.990
[Laura sighs]

513
00:35:17.073 --> 00:35:18.742
This is so upsetting.

514
00:35:18.825 --> 00:35:20.744
And so infuriating as well.

515
00:35:20.827 --> 00:35:21.911
It's not fair.

516
00:35:22.412 --> 00:35:23.747
Ah, I'm sorry, but…

517
00:35:23.830 --> 00:35:27.584
it's His Majesty having an affair,
it's not Her Majesty's fault at all.

518
00:35:27.667 --> 00:35:30.253
And yet malicious rumors
surround her instead.

519
00:35:30.337 --> 00:35:32.756
Those people,
they do whatever they please,

520
00:35:32.839 --> 00:35:35.425
but Her Majesty has to be careful.

521
00:35:35.508 --> 00:35:38.637
She's innocent.
It's that Rashta woman's fault.

522
00:35:38.720 --> 00:35:40.972
I just… hate her so much.

523
00:35:41.556 --> 00:35:42.807
No! Is it really?

524
00:35:42.891 --> 00:35:45.435
-Yes, I'm telling you!
-[laughs] No way!

525
00:35:46.061 --> 00:35:47.062
I know.

526
00:35:47.145 --> 00:35:49.648
It's not certain, so keep it to yourself.

527
00:35:49.731 --> 00:35:50.774
-All right? Shh!
-All right.

528
00:35:52.359 --> 00:35:54.277
Heinrey the Prince and Her Majesty…

529
00:35:54.361 --> 00:35:55.695
-[speaks indistinctly]
-All right.

530
00:35:55.779 --> 00:35:56.905
Yes, all right.

531
00:35:56.988 --> 00:35:58.448
-Oh! You're back!
-[Kisia] You're back!

532
00:36:02.702 --> 00:36:03.953
[Rashta sighs heavily]

533
00:36:04.871 --> 00:36:05.914
This is hard.

534
00:36:05.997 --> 00:36:08.291
[chuckles] Did you enjoy yourself?

535
00:36:08.375 --> 00:36:09.542
How was the banquet?

536
00:36:09.626 --> 00:36:13.380
[sighs] The men talked about war,
so it was a bit boring.

537
00:36:14.464 --> 00:36:17.384
I heard people saying
today's banquet was more enjoyable

538
00:36:17.467 --> 00:36:19.803
because Prince Heinrey brought
an amusing story with him.

539
00:36:19.886 --> 00:36:21.388
Was that not true?

540
00:36:22.055 --> 00:36:25.767
Well, if it was a party Prince Heinrey
had been to, it would have.

541
00:36:26.351 --> 00:36:27.894
That would have been fun.

542
00:36:27.977 --> 00:36:29.813
With loads more guests, too.

543
00:36:31.481 --> 00:36:35.443
[sighs] I only hope people will come
to Rashta's party as well.

544
00:36:35.527 --> 00:36:36.945
I'm worried.

545
00:36:37.028 --> 00:36:41.908
What if it's empty like Duke Ristore's
and becomes a total failure?

546
00:36:45.912 --> 00:36:46.913
So then…

547
00:36:47.455 --> 00:36:48.832
these amusing things.

548
00:36:48.915 --> 00:36:50.959
You must tell me everything that was said.

549
00:36:51.042 --> 00:36:52.085
Here is what I've heard.

550
00:36:52.168 --> 00:36:54.212
There's someone in the Eastern Empire

551
00:36:54.295 --> 00:36:56.631
with whom he has been
exchanging secret letters.

552
00:36:56.715 --> 00:36:58.633
Ooh! Romantic!

553
00:36:58.717 --> 00:37:01.553
But he's been searching for the person
he exchanged letters with,

554
00:37:01.636 --> 00:37:03.388
and no one has come forward yet,

555
00:37:03.471 --> 00:37:05.390
and he's terribly anxious about it all.

556
00:37:05.974 --> 00:37:07.350
Is that so?

557
00:37:08.268 --> 00:37:09.561
A lady…

558
00:37:10.145 --> 00:37:14.065
whose face, name,
and status he doesn't know.

559
00:37:15.775 --> 00:37:18.653
They say the person he's writing to

560
00:37:18.737 --> 00:37:21.114
could even be Her Majesty
the Empress herself!

561
00:37:21.197 --> 00:37:23.074
We were just talking about it.

562
00:37:23.158 --> 00:37:24.492
Hey!

563
00:37:24.576 --> 00:37:26.202
-What?
-[♪ ominous music playing]

564
00:37:26.286 --> 00:37:27.954
It might not be true.

565
00:37:29.914 --> 00:37:31.124
What are you both saying?

566
00:37:35.712 --> 00:37:37.046
[hesitatingly] Well…

567
00:37:39.758 --> 00:37:41.050
I heard it, too.

568
00:37:41.134 --> 00:37:42.886
It's just I have this cousin…

569
00:37:43.553 --> 00:37:46.181
He works at the Western Palace,
and apparently…

570
00:37:46.264 --> 00:37:51.895
a bird flew to Her Majesty
with a letter tied to its ankle.

571
00:37:54.439 --> 00:37:55.815
Uh-huh…

572
00:37:59.486 --> 00:38:03.156
Please can you find out what was written
on all of the letters?

573
00:38:03.239 --> 00:38:05.575
MARCHIONESS HELENA DE MONTCLAIR
CIRCE ILONA LIAN

574
00:38:13.041 --> 00:38:14.751
[clicks, clatters]

575
00:38:35.939 --> 00:38:37.440
Are you enjoying your stay?

576
00:38:38.566 --> 00:38:40.109
Yes, I am, thank you.

577
00:38:40.193 --> 00:38:42.153
It's lovely, thanks to you, Your Majesty.

578
00:38:42.695 --> 00:38:43.696
That's wonderful.

579
00:38:44.697 --> 00:38:46.866
I heard there's someone
you're searching for.

580
00:38:48.243 --> 00:38:49.244
Yes.

581
00:38:49.953 --> 00:38:52.330
I very much wish to find them.

582
00:38:54.165 --> 00:38:56.376
Why is their discovery so important?

583
00:38:57.669 --> 00:38:58.962
You have many friends.

584
00:38:59.504 --> 00:39:00.588
They dote on you.

585
00:39:01.172 --> 00:39:03.216
You're always surrounded by people.

586
00:39:05.051 --> 00:39:06.594
You can still feel lonely…

587
00:39:07.512 --> 00:39:08.930
even if you're surrounded.

588
00:39:11.266 --> 00:39:13.268
You already know that, Your Majesty.

589
00:39:24.988 --> 00:39:27.323
If you are sharing your thoughts
through these letters…

590
00:39:28.658 --> 00:39:29.993
why meet at all?

591
00:39:32.453 --> 00:39:34.247
-They are too special.
-[♪ yearning music playing]

592
00:39:34.330 --> 00:39:35.832
I must meet that person.

593
00:39:40.420 --> 00:39:41.921
I pray they feel the same.

594
00:39:44.048 --> 00:39:47.051
I've never before revealed
my true feelings without pretense.

595
00:39:49.762 --> 00:39:53.182
It was also nice to let my guard down
and share jokes.

596
00:39:54.475 --> 00:39:55.476
I've never…

597
00:39:56.728 --> 00:39:58.688
felt my heart flutter like that.

598
00:40:01.441 --> 00:40:02.483
These letters…

599
00:40:03.526 --> 00:40:05.987
they are precious, and so is their author.

600
00:40:07.196 --> 00:40:08.573
I have to meet them.

601
00:40:16.456 --> 00:40:18.458
[♪ music continues]

602
00:41:15.014 --> 00:41:16.349
[♪ music continues]

603
00:41:32.115 --> 00:41:33.491
[gentle chiming]

604
00:41:41.416 --> 00:41:42.542
[sighs]

605
00:41:42.625 --> 00:41:45.169
[♪ captivating music playing]

606
00:42:02.478 --> 00:42:04.522
[♪ music swells]

607
00:42:34.302 --> 00:42:35.845
[♪ music continues]

608
00:43:24.519 --> 00:43:26.270
[♪ music slows down]

609
00:43:33.736 --> 00:43:35.488
[♪ music fades]

610
00:43:43.579 --> 00:43:45.581
[♪ gentle music playing]

611
00:43:48.417 --> 00:43:49.460
[clinking softly]

612
00:44:05.518 --> 00:44:06.644
[exhales softly]

613
00:44:14.443 --> 00:44:15.820
[♪ music continues]

614
00:44:33.713 --> 00:44:35.131
[inhales deeply]

615
00:44:35.214 --> 00:44:36.257
Ah!

616
00:44:36.340 --> 00:44:37.425
[chuckles softly]

617
00:44:39.844 --> 00:44:42.680
Your tea is getting cold.
Will you come and drink it?

618
00:44:43.181 --> 00:44:44.390
[sighs heavily]

619
00:44:47.351 --> 00:44:49.854
[exasperated sigh]
I'm not letting mine go cold.

620
00:44:51.397 --> 00:44:52.857
[knock on door]

621
00:44:55.151 --> 00:44:57.111
Yes, come in.

622
00:44:59.363 --> 00:45:00.489
[door closes]

623
00:45:00.573 --> 00:45:03.576
There is someone waiting
for Prince Heinrey in the lobby.

624
00:45:06.537 --> 00:45:07.538
Who is it?

625
00:45:07.622 --> 00:45:09.498
"A fate that was lost," Majesty.

626
00:45:09.582 --> 00:45:10.625
[♪ exciting music playing]

627
00:45:10.708 --> 00:45:11.709
Oh?

628
00:45:12.376 --> 00:45:13.419
Wha…

629
00:45:14.295 --> 00:45:16.464
-Your Highness? What?
-[Heinrey] Where did it go? McKenna!

630
00:45:16.547 --> 00:45:17.924
[McKenna] What's that?
What are you looking for?

631
00:45:18.007 --> 00:45:19.008
-Why--
-McKenna, where is it?

632
00:45:19.091 --> 00:45:20.301
-Whoa, whoa, whoa.
-You know the jacket.

633
00:45:20.384 --> 00:45:21.427
-The gold jacket?
-Oh!

634
00:45:21.510 --> 00:45:22.720
Yes, you know the one that's… And that's…

635
00:45:22.803 --> 00:45:23.930
-The one that's a lot?
-Right!

636
00:45:24.013 --> 00:45:25.056
-The gappy one, ah!
-Yes.

637
00:45:25.139 --> 00:45:26.349
At the end, on the right.

638
00:45:26.974 --> 00:45:28.100
Go and get it.

639
00:45:28.184 --> 00:45:29.602
-[McKenna] Argh!
-Let's go.

640
00:45:29.685 --> 00:45:32.230
It's a wonder you can even
wash your own face, honestly.

641
00:45:33.022 --> 00:45:34.232
-[knocks on door]
-[noblewoman] Come out!

642
00:45:34.315 --> 00:45:35.524
Prince Heinrey's letter friend is here!

643
00:45:35.608 --> 00:45:37.109
Prince Heinrey's letter friend
has appeared!

644
00:45:37.193 --> 00:45:38.778
Prince Heinrey's letter friend has come.

645
00:45:38.861 --> 00:45:40.154
Everyone, come on out!

646
00:45:40.238 --> 00:45:42.531
[♪ music intensifies]

647
00:46:04.929 --> 00:46:06.389
[footsteps approaching]

648
00:46:08.557 --> 00:46:11.102
[nobleman] Don't you think
Prince Heinrey is so dashing?

649
00:46:11.185 --> 00:46:12.228
[exhales]

650
00:46:12.979 --> 00:46:14.480
[noblewoman] Look at that jacket!

651
00:46:17.900 --> 00:46:19.068
[exhales]

652
00:46:27.743 --> 00:46:29.745
[♪ dramatic music playing]

653
00:46:47.138 --> 00:46:50.099
Your Highness, I heard
that you have searched ardently.

654
00:46:52.476 --> 00:46:54.812
I am the secret pen pal
you've been writing to.

655
00:46:55.688 --> 00:46:58.274
Your "lost fate", and you found me now.

656
00:46:59.233 --> 00:47:01.277
[♪ music continues]

657
00:47:07.533 --> 00:47:09.035
[crowd clapping]

658
00:47:10.619 --> 00:47:12.621
[♪ music swells]

659
00:47:24.216 --> 00:47:26.469
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

660
00:47:26.927 --> 00:47:27.928
[♪ music fades]

661
00:47:29.430 --> 00:47:31.432
[♪ closing theme music playing]

